# The Design of Databases and Other Information Resources for Humanities Scholars: The Getty Online Searching Project Report No. 4.

**Authors:** Bates, Marcia J.

## Abstract
Based on the results of a two-year study conducted by the Getty Art History Information Program of online searching by humanities scholars, implications are drawn for the design of information products. Topics include characteristics of humanities scholars; design and content of databases; indexing vocabulary; and interfaces and command languages. (Author/DGM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ534425

